  "problem_number": "OWR-17471-009",
  "title": "Uniform Perfectness of Four-Manifold Diffeomorphism Groups",
  "statement": "Are there closed orientable smooth $4$-manifolds $M$ for which the identity component $\\operatorname{Diff}_0(M)$ is not uniformly perfect?",
  "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [Low-dimensional Topology (2021), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2020/8, pp. 465--516](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/8)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-22)\n\n**Status:** open\n\n**Assessment.** Uniform perfectness is proved in broad dimensions but the four-dimensional identity component remains an explicit unresolved exception in the literature.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [Fukui and Rybicki, uniform perfectness in even dimensions](https://ems.press/journals/cmh/articles/10844)\n- [Oberwolfach Report 8/2020](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/8)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
